# pyro_disturbance

- Label: Pyro Disturbance Force
- Category: Copernicus (`Cop`), Houdini 22.0.368
- Inputs: 0 to 5
- Parameters: 67 (exact, read from Houdini by hython)
- Used by the height graph: no

## Feature summary (web, SideFX reference)

- Source: https://www.sidefx.com/docs/houdini/nodes/cop/pyro_disturbance.html
- Summary (EN): Applies disturbance to a velocity VDB to break up still air. It adds small noisy forces to a smoke or fire velocity field; the forces cancel out over time, so overall motion and shape are preserved. Output is v, the disturbed Vector VDB.
- Résumé (FR) : Pyro Disturbance ajoute de petites forces bruitées à un champ de vitesse pour casser l'air immobile, en conservant le mouvement global.

- Inputs meaning: ["v: Vector VDB of the incoming velocities", "threshold (optional): Float or Vector VDB limiting where the effect applies; a Vector VDB is read by its length", "control (optional): Float or Vector VDB smoothly scaling the effect; a Vector VDB is read by its length"]

- Key parameters: ["Operation: Set replaces velocities with the disturbance; Add adds it to existing velocity; Rotate turns existing velocities toward random directions without changing their length", "Mode: Continuous gives each voxel its own random vector for voxel-scale detail; Block-Based layers blockwise-constant noise for larger structured patterns", "Disturbance (Strength): force strength; with Rotate, the speed at which vectors turn", "Reference Scale: normalizes the force against scene and voxel size; set once for the scene scale", "Block Size, Pulse Length: largest noise block and hold time of each pattern (Block-Based only)", "Max Octaves, Lacunarity, Roughness: number of noise layers, block-size ratio, amplitude ratio (Block-Based only)", "Mask by Threshold Field, Mask by Control Field, Mask along Axis: spatial limits on the effect"]

- Caveats: ["Requires DOP-level permissions; not in Houdini Core, only in Houdini FX, Apprentice, Indie and Education", "In Continuous mode, a very small voxel size can produce a noisy, undesirable look", "Using density as the threshold input keeps the disturbance out of empty areas so visible smoke is not affected"]

